verses.tf_en:
① **«سُبْحَانَ الَّذِی أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَیْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى»** — *(Exalted is He Who took His Servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque)* — Theological Reality & Creed of Ahl al-Sunnah wal-Jama'ah: The opening of Surah Al-Isra (also named Surah Bani Isra'il and Surah Subhan) celebrates the supreme, miraculous journey of the Master of Creation, Prophet Muhammad ﷺ—*Al-Isra' wal-Mi'raj*. The term *«سُبْحٰنَ»* proclaims the absolute transcendence, omnipotence, and purity of Allah, signaling that a wondrous event beyond all human capability and physical laws is being described. The term *«بِعَبْدِهٖ»* (His special servant) is the highest honorific conferred upon the Prophet ﷺ, proving indisputably that the journey was performed **in a physical body united with his blessed soul (*bi-jasadihi wa-ruhihi*) in a fully awake state (*yaqazatan*)**, and not merely in a dream or spiritual vision; for sleep journeys do not require divine glorification (*Tasbih*) nor would they provoke the vehement denial and amazement of the Meccan pagans. The journey from the Ka'bah (*al-Masjid al-Haram*) in Mecca across hundreds of miles to Jerusalem (*al-Masjid al-Aqsa*) occurred in a mere fraction of a single night (*Laylan*);
② **«الَّذِیْ بٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهٗ لِنُرِیَهٗ مِنْ اٰیٰتِنَا»** — *(whose surroundings We have blessed, in order that We might show him of Our signs)* — surrounding the sacred sanctuary of Jerusalem with spiritual blessings (the homeland, tombs, and prayer-places of thousands of prophets) and earthly fertility; and this monumental journey was conducted in order that Allah might display to His Beloved Habib ﷺ His greatest cosmological, angelic, and divine signs (*Ayatina*), elevating him through the seven heavens, past the *Sidrat al-Muntaha*, to the transcendent Station of Proximity (*Qaba Qawsayn*);
③ **«اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِیْعُ الْبَصِیْرُ»** — *(Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing)* — Truly Allah is All-Hearing of the prayers of His Messenger ﷺ and All-Seeing of his sublime spiritual fitness for this supreme cosmic intimacy. Note: In classical Sunni jurisprudence and creed, accepting the bodily journey of *Al-Isra* to Jerusalem is an absolute article of faith proven by explicit Quranic text (whoever denies it commits disbelief, *kufr*); while accepting the ascension (*Mi'raj*) to the heavens is established by mass-transmitted (*Mutawatir*) authentic Hadith, and its denier is a severe heretic and innovator (*fasiq / dal*).

① **«اِنْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ وَاِنْ اَسَاْتُمْ فَلَهَا»** — *(If you do good, you do good for your own souls; and if you do evil, it is against them)* — If you practice righteousness, uphold divine covenants, and obey the Prophets, the blessings and honor will accrue to your own benefit in this world and the next; whereas if you commit tyranny, transgress, and rebel, the calamitous consequences will rebound solely upon your own heads;
② **«فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ الْآخِرَةِ لِیَسُوءُوا وُجُوهَكُمْ»** — *(then when the promise of the second came to pass, [We sent enemies] to disfigure your faces)* — And when the foretold epoch of your second major corruption arrived—when the Children of Israel breached their covenants anew, martyred Prophet Zakariyya ('alayhis-salam) and Prophet Yahya ('alayhis-salam), and maliciously plotted to crucify Prophet 'Isa ('alayhis-salam)—Allah unleashed upon them ruthless foreign conquerors (the Roman forces led by Titus);
③ **«وَلِیَدْخُلُوا الْمَسْجِدَ كَمَا دَخَلُوْهُ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّلِیُتَبِّرُوْا مَا عَلَوْا تَتْبِیْرًا»** — *(and to enter the Mosque as they had entered it the first time, and to utterly demolish whatever they conquered)* — so the invaders humiliated them, disfiguring their faces with terror and grief, stormed the Holy Sanctuary of Bayt al-Maqdis just as the Babylonians had done previously, burned the Temple, massacred tens of thousands, and completely annihilated everything that fell beneath their dominion.

① **«وَجَعَلْنَا اللَّیْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ آیَتَیْنِ ۖ فَمَحَوْنَا آیَةَ اللَّیْلِ وَجَعَلْنَا آیَةَ النَّهَارِ مُبْصِرَةً»** — *(And We made the night and the day as two signs: We erased the sign of the night and made the sign of the day illuminating)* — We established the alternation of night and day as two majestic signs of Our creative power and divine unity: We veiled the sign of the night in darkness and coolness so that creation might rest, slumber, and rejuvenate; while We made the sign of the day radiant with sunlight so that mankind may actively see, move, and work;
② **«لِّتَبْتَغُوْا فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِیْنَ وَالْحِسَابَ»** — *(so that you may seek bounty from your Lord and know the number of years and the reckoning)* — enabling you to pursue lawful livelihood (*Rizq Halal*) and track the passage of time, months, and calendar years necessary for commercial contracts and religious rites;
③ **«وَكُلَّ شَیْءٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ تَفْصِیْلًا»** — *(and everything We have explained distinctly in detail)* — and We have expounded every vital reality, doctrinal truth, and legal command in the Holy Quran with crystal-clear elucidation.

① **«مَنِ اهْتَدٰی فَاِنَّمَا یَهْتَدِیْ لِنَفْسِهٖ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا یَضِلُّ عَلَیْهَا»** — *(Whoever is guided is only guided for his own soul, and whoever strays only strays to its detriment)* — Whoever embraces divine guidance and adheres to the straight path secures their own ultimate felicity and eternal salvation; whereas whoever rejects the truth and strays into delusion brings ruin and destruction solely upon their own being;
② **«وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰی»** — *(and no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another)* — and according to the absolute justice of Allah, no burdened soul shall bear the guilt, sins, or punishment of any other soul;
③ **«وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِیْنَ حَتّٰی نَبْعَثَ رَسُوْلًا»** — *(and We never punish until We have dispatched a Messenger)* — and out of divine mercy, We never afflict any community or individual with punishment until We have sent an exalted Messenger to convey the clear proofs of revelation and establish the divine argument (*Iqamat al-Hujjah*).

① **«وَقَضٰی رَبُّكَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِیَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَیْنِ اِحْسَانًا»** — *(And your Lord has decreed that you worship none but Him, and show utmost kindness to parents)* — The Divine Charter of Filial Piety: Your Lord has issued an absolute, non-negotiable decree: that you dedicate worship, devotion, and servitude exclusively to Him alone, and immediately conjoined with His divine right, that you treat your parents with profound excellence, tenderness, financial support, and obedience (*Ihsan*);
② **«اِمَّا یَبْلُغَنَّ عِنْدَكَ الْكِبَرَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَوْ كِلٰهُمَا فَلَا تَقُلْ لَّهُمَاۤ اُفٍّ وَّلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا»** — *(If one or both of them attain old age in your care, do not say to them so much as "Uff" and do not rebuke them)* — If either of them, or both, reach the vulnerability, fragility, and emotional sensitivity of old age while under your guardianship, do not utter even the slightest sigh of irritation, impatience, or annoyance ("Uff!"), nor scold, reprimand, or raise your voice against them;
③ **«وَقُلْ لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِیْمًا»** — *(and speak to them a noble, honorable word)* — rather, converse with them at all times with the utmost reverence, gentleness, affection, and veneration, honoring them as a humble servant addresses an exalted benefactor. Classical Hanafi scholars emphasize that calling parents by their personal names directly or looking at them with a furrowed brow is strictly forbidden.

① **«وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِیْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ»** — *(And do not kill the soul which Allah has sanctified, except with legitimate right)* — Human life is divinely consecrated and inviolable; therefore, no life may be terminated except through strict, lawful judicial authority based upon explicit Shariah grounds (such as mandatory retribution for deliberate murder, high treason against the Muslim state, or severe crimes established through due process);
② **«وَمَنْ قُتِلَ مَظْلُوْمًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِیِّهٖ سُلْطٰنًا»** — *(and whoever is slain wrongfully, We have given his legal heir authority)* — and whoever is murdered unjustly, We have granted his lawful heir (*Wali al-Dam*) legal authority to demand capital retribution (*Qisas*) through the courts or accept financial blood-money (*Diyah*) or grant gratuitous pardon;
③ **«فَلَا یُسْرِفْ فِّی الْقَتْلِ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مَنْصُوْرًا»** — *(so let him not exceed limits in slaying; indeed, he is already aided)* — but the heir must not exceed the bounds of justice—such as killing innocent relatives of the murderer or mutilating the corpse, as was customary during the pre-Islamic Jahiliyyah; for the divine law itself guarantees him aid and justice.

① **«تُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمٰوٰتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِیْهِنَّ»** — *(The seven heavens and the earth and all beings within them declare His glory)* — All existence—the seven expanses of the heavens, the planetary earth, and every inhabitant within them, from luminous angels to physical creatures—proclaims the pristine holiness and majestic perfection of Almighty Allah;
② **«وَاِنْ مِّنْ شَیْءٍ اِلَّا یُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تَفْقَهُوْنَ تَسْبِیْحَهُمْ»** — *(and there is not a single thing but glorifies Him with praise, but you do not understand their glorification)* — Authentic Sunnah & Universal Tasbih: Not a single entity in creation—whether living beings, vegetation, mountains, minerals, or inanimate stones—fails to celebrate His praise in actual, articulate speech appropriate to its nature; though ordinary humans lack the auditory and spiritual perception to comprehend their glorification. The classical Hadith masters record that the Sahabah heard the food glorifying Allah while eating with the Prophet ﷺ, the crying palm trunk (*Ustuwanah Hannanah*) wept aloud for the Prophet ﷺ in his mosque, and the stones of Mecca audibly offered Salam to him;
③ **«اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حَلِیْمًا غَفُوْرًا»** — *(indeed, He is ever Clement, Oft-Forgiving)* — for despite the insolence of mankind in withholding gratitude and uttering blasphemies, Allah does not immediately strike them with punishment, exercising supreme forbearance (*Halim*) and granting ample opportunity for forgiveness (*Ghafur*).

① **«اَوْ خَلْقًا مِّمَّا یَكْبُرُ فِیْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ»** — *(Or some creation which is even greater in your estimation!)* — Or become something even more immense, durable, and defying of life in your imaginations (such as the heavens or mountains);
② **«فَسَیَقُوْلُوْنَ مَنْ یُّعِیْدُنَا قُلِ الَّذِیْ فَطَرَكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ»** — *(Then they will ask: "Who will bring us back?" Say: "He Who created you the first time!")* — When they persistently object: "Who could possibly possess the power to recreate us from nothing?", say to them: "The very same Almighty Creator Who brought you into existence from sheer non-existence the first time! For He Who initiated creation can easily restore it";
③ **«فَسَیُنْغِضُوْنَ اِلَیْكَ رُءُوْسَهُمْ وَیَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰی هُوَ قُلْ عَسٰۤی اَنْ یَّكُوْنَ قَرِیْبًا»** — *(Then they will mockingly shake their heads at you and say: "When will that be?" Say: "Perhaps it is very near!")* — Cornered by this irrefutable proof, they will shake their heads in sarcastic derision and ask: "When exactly will this resurrection occur?" Tell them: "It may well be imminent; for everything that is destined to arrive is near at hand."

① **«وَاِذْ قُلْنَا لَكَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ اَحَاطَ بِالنَّاسِ»** — *(And recall when We told you [O Beloved Prophet]: "Indeed, your Lord encompasses all mankind")* — Remember when We assured you, O Beloved Prophet ﷺ, that your Lord encompasses all mankind within His irresistible power, knowledge, and sovereign protection; therefore, proclaim the divine message fearlessly, for no enemy can thwart your mission;
② **«وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّءْیَا الَّتِیْۤ اَرَیْنٰكَ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلنَّاسِ»** — *(and We did not make the vision which We showed you except as a trial for mankind)* — Bodily Reality of Mi'raj: The glorious vision (*Al-Ru'ya*) displayed to the Holy Prophet ﷺ was not an ordinary nocturnal dream, but the **actual physical observation with waking eyes (*Ru'yat al-'Ayn yaqazatan*)** during the Night of Heavenly Ascension (*Al-Isra' wal-Mi'raj*), traversing the celestial spheres and witnessing the divine signs. It served as a crucible of faith (*Fitnah*), wherein the steadfast believers rejoiced while the skeptical disbelievers mocked and fell into deeper delusion;
③ **«وَالشَّجَرَةَ الْمَلْعُوْنَةَ فِی الْقُرْاٰنِ وَنُخَوِّفُهُمْ فَمَا یَزِیْدُهُمْ اِلَّا طُغْیَانًا كَبِیْرًا»** — *(and likewise the tree cursed in the Qur'an; and We warn them, yet it increases them in nothing but monstrous rebellion)* — and likewise the tree cursed in the Quran—the horrific Tree of Zaqqum growing out of the base of Hellfire—became a test when Abu Jahl mockingly questioned how a tree could grow in fire; yet despite all divine warnings, the obstinate pagans only plunge into colossal, brazen transgression.

verses.tf_bn:
① **«وَاسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُمْ بِصَوْتِكَ»** — ‘এবং তোর আওয়াজ দ্বারা (কুপ্ররোচনা, অনর্থক অশ্লীল গান-বাজনা, নিষিদ্ধ বাদ্যযন্ত্র ও আল্লাহর অবাধ্যতার ডাক) তাদের মধ্যে যাকে পারো বিভ্রান্ত ও পদস্খলিত করো; 
② **«وَاَجْلِبْ عَلَیْهِمْ بِخَیْلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ»** — এবং তাদের বিরুদ্ধে চড়িয়ে আনো তোমার অশ্বারোহী ও পদাতিক বাহিনীকে (অর্থাৎ যাবতীয় বাহ্যিক ও মানসিক সহযোগী শক্তিকে); 
③ **«وَشَارِكْهُمْ فِی الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَوْلَادِ»** — আর তাদের সম্পদে (সুদ, ঘুষ, চুরি, আত্মসাৎ ও হারামে ব্যয় করা) এবং সন্তানে (ব্যভিচার, জারজ সন্তান ও কুফরী তরবিয়তে) অংশীদার হয়ে যাও; 
④ **«وَعِدْهُمْ وَمَا یَعِدُهُمُ الشَّیْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا»** — এবং তাদের মিথ্যা আশ্বাস দাও।’ আর শয়তানের সমস্ত প্রতিশ্রুতি কেবলই ধোঁকা ও প্রতারণা বই কিছুই নয়।

verses.tf_en:
① **«وَاسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُمْ بِصَوْتِكَ»** — *(And entice whomsoever you can of them with your voice)* — "Exert all your cunning to allure whomsoever you can with your seductive voice—including illicit calls, sinful whisperings, frivolous music, seductive songs, and incitements to vanity;
② **«وَاَجْلِبْ عَلَیْهِمْ بِخَیْلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ»** — *(and rally against them your cavalry and your infantry)* — and summon against them all your mounted and foot soldiers (every physical, psychological, and institutional agency of evil);
③ **«وَشَارِكْهُمْ فِی الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَوْلَادِ»** — *(and share with them in their wealth and children)* — and become an accomplice in their wealth (by tempting them toward usury, bribery, theft, and squandering in sinful venues) and in their offspring (through adultery, illegitimate children, and pagan indoctrination);
④ **«وَعِدْهُمْ وَمَا یَعِدُهُمُ الشَّیْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا»** — *(and make promises to them"; yet Satan promises them nothing except delusion)* — and lure them with false promises of worldly grandeur and impunity from the Hereafter"; yet every single promise of Satan is sheer deception and hollow fantasy.

① **«اَمْ اَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ یُّعِیْدَكُمْ فِیْهِ تَارَةً اُخْرٰی»** — *(Or do you feel secure that He will not send you back into it [the sea] a second time)* — Or have you obtained an assurance that circumstances will never compel you to embark upon the deep ocean once again;
② **«فَیُرْسِلَ عَلَیْكُمْ قَاصِفًا مِّنَ الرِّیْحِ فَیُغْرِقَكُمْ بِمَا كَفَرْتُمْ»** — *(and unleash upon you a ship-shattering hurricane and drown you for your disbelief)* — whereupon He would unleash upon you a devastating, vessel-shattering tempest (*Qasifam min ar-rih*), plunging you into watery oblivion as a just retribution for your persistent ingratitude and disbelief;
③ **«ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْا لَكُمْ عَلَیْنَا بِهٖ تَبِیْعًا»** — *(then you will not find for yourselves any prosecutor against Us on that account?)* — and you would find no champion or seeker of blood-vengeance to interrogate Us or demand reckoning for your destruction.

verses.tf_bn:
① **«وَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِیْۤ اٰدَمَ وَحَمَلْنٰهُمْ فِی الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ»** — বনী আদমের অনন্য মর্যাদা: নিশ্চয় আমি আদম সন্তানকে প্রভূত সম্মান দান করেছি (বিবেক-বুদ্ধি, বাকশক্তি, সুন্দর গঠন, সৃষ্টির ওপর কর্তৃত্ব ও চিন্তাশক্তি প্রদানের মাধ্যমে), এবং তাদেরকে জল ও স্থলে বিভিন্ন বাহনে আরোহণের ব্যবস্থা করে দিয়েছি; 
② **«وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّیِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلٰی كَثِیْرٍ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقْنَا تَفْضِیْلًا»** — এবং তাদেরকে উত্তম, সুস্বাদু ও পবিত্র খাদ্যসামগ্রী দ্বারা রিযিক দিয়েছি এবং আমার অগণিত সৃষ্টির ওপর শ্রেষ্ঠত্ব ও মর্যাদা দান করেছি। 
আক্বীদা ও সূক্ষ্ম তত্ত্ব: মুফাসসিরীনের সর্বসম্মত সিদ্ধান্ত অনুযায়ী আম্বিয়ায়ে কিরাম ফেরেশতাকুলের প্রধানদের অপেক্ষাও শ্রেষ্ঠ এবং সাধারণ মুমিন ও সালেহীনগণ সাধারণ ফেরেশতাদের অপেক্ষাও আল্লাহর নিকট অধিক সম্মানিত। কারণ ফেরেশতাদের মাঝে কেবল বিবেক রয়েছে কিন্তু প্রবৃত্তি নেই, জন্তু-জানোয়ারের মাঝে প্রবৃত্তি রয়েছে কিন্তু বিবেক নেই; পক্ষান্তরে মানুষের মধ্যে উভয়টি রয়েছে—অতএব যে মানুষ স্বীয় প্রবৃত্তিকে দমন করে বিবেকের মাধ্যমে আল্লাহর অনুগত হয়, সে ফেরেশতা অপেক্ষাও উচ্চমর্যাদায় আসীন হয়।

① **«وَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِیْ لَمْ یَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا»** — আয়াতুল ইয্য (মর্যাদার মহাসূত্র): এবং বলুন, সমস্ত প্রশংসা সেই মহান আল্লাহর—যিনি নিজের জন্য কোনো সন্তান গ্রহণ করেননি (ইহুদী, খ্রিষ্টান ও মুশরিকদের মিথ্যা দাবির অবসান); 
② **«وَّلَمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِیْكٌ فِی الْمُلْكِ»** — এবং বিশ্বজাহানের রাজত্ব ও কর্তৃত্বে যাঁর কোনো অংশীদার নেই; 
③ **«وَلَمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِیٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِیْرًا»** — এবং দুর্বলতার কারণে যাঁর কোনো সাহায্যকারী বা পৃষ্ঠপোষকের মুখাপেক্ষিতা নেই; এবং তাঁর অনুপম সুউচ্চ মহিমা ঘোষণার জন্য সর্বান্তঃকরণে তাঁর তাকবীর ধ্বনিত করুন (‘আল্লাহু আকবার’ পাঠ করুন)। 
ফযীলত ও বরকত: এই আয়াতকে ‘আয়াতুল ইয্য’ (মর্যাদার আয়াত) বলা হয়। হযরত আবদুল মুত্তালিবের বংশধরেরা সন্তানদের কথা ফোটার পর সর্বপ্রথম এই মোবারক আয়াতটি শিক্ষা দিতেন। সহীহ হাদীস শরীফে এসেছে, কিয়ামতের দিন জান্নাতের দিকে সর্বপ্রথম তাদেরকে আহ্বান জানানো হবে যারা সুখে-দুঃখে সর্বদা আল্লাহর হামদ ও শোকর আদায় করত।

verses.tf_en:
① **«وَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِیْ لَمْ یَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا»** (And say: “All praise belongs to Allah, Who has not taken a son) — *Ayat al-'Izz* (The Verse of Supreme Majesty): Proclaim, O Beloved Prophet ﷺ: All absolute praise belongs exclusively to Allah, Who is transcendent above having progeny, entirely refuting the blasphemous fabrications of the Christians, Jews, and pagan Arabs;
② **«وَّلَمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِیْكٌ فِی الْمُلْكِ»** (and has no partner in His dominion) — Who possesses absolute, unshared sovereignty over the cosmos, with zero partners in His essence, attributes, or cosmic lordship;
③ **«وَلَمْ یَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِیٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِیْرًا»** (and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence”) — Who requires no patron, guardian, or ally out of vulnerability or need, for He is the Self-Sufficient Sustainer of all existence (*Al-Qayyum*); and glorify His supreme majesty with ceaseless Takbir (*Allahu Akbar*).
*Virtues of Ayat al-'Izz*:
This concluding verse of Surah al-Isra is famously designated as the ‘Verse of Supreme Majesty’ (*Ayat al-'Izz*). The noble clan of 'Abd al-Muttalib upheld the tradition of teaching this profound verse to every child as soon as they began to speak. It seals Surah al-Isra with the purest exposition of Islamic monotheism (*Tawhid*), confirming that praise, sovereignty, and unyielding greatness belong to Allah alone.
